# Fixed 2026-09-30, defect 130's class, lane recovery-b1 (lane X4's finding
# n2). Symptom: a case's fields in braces, `circle {` over `r f64,` over `},`
# inside a braced variant, cost *expected a case name, found `{`* and the
# fields went unread, `r f64` never told; in an indented variant the `}`
# below cost a second `expected_case`, and so did braces alone on the line
# below a case, Allman's style. Cause: nothing past a case's name read braces
# as its fields, where a record's in braces were read. Now the `{` is told
# once, as any junk past a case's name is, the fields are read through the
# view of the braces (`selfhost/parse/braced_lines.hero`), and what stands
# past the `}` on its line is junk past the case
# (`selfhost/parse/member_lines.hero`).

variant Shape {  #~ expected_end_of_line
    circle {  #~ expected_end_of_line
        r f64,  #~ expected_field_type
    },
    square  #~ expected_end_of_line
}

variant Figure
    ring {  #~ expected_end_of_line
        r: f64
        w f64  #~ expected_field_type
    }
    dot { x: f64, y f64 }  #~ expected_end_of_line expected_field_type
    empty {}  #~ expected_end_of_line
    arc
    {  #~ expected_case
        a f64  #~ expected_field_type
    }
    blob { r: f64 } x  #~ expected_end_of_line expected_end_of_line
    last

function main()
    print(1)

# Read again 2026-10-01, lane recovery-b5 (ruling 1, `selfhost/brace_layout.hero`):
# the lexer lays out a body's braces as the block their fix leaves, so the
# lines in them are judged as without the braces. `square,` is told as it is
# with no braces, the variant's one `,` report, certain, and the `},` above it
# goes with its `}`; the case's own braces are read as the block below the
# case, and its fields' mistakes are told as before. `check --apply` deletes
# the `,` (`.applied`).
